From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>
Sent: Saturday, September 5, 2026 3:56 PM
To: GAUTHIER Katie * OPRD <katie.gauthier@oprd.oregon.gov>; PUBLICRECORDS O=
prd * OPRD <oprd.publicrecords@oprd.oregon.gov>
Cc: COLLIER JR * OPRD <jr.collier@oprd.oregon.gov>; SUMPTION Lisa * OPRD <l=
isa.sumption@oprd.oregon.gov>; PUBLICCOMMENT Oprc * OPRD <oprc.publiccommen=
t@oprd.oregon.gov>; Governor Kotek * GOV <governor.kotek@oregon.gov>
Subject: Public records request under ORS 192.311 to 192.478



This is a request under the Oregon Public Records Law. It is narrow by desi=
gn and concerns two custodians only.



I am Robert Samuel White, date of birth April 11, 1977. I served as an unpa=
id volunteer with the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department at Jessie M. H=
oneyman Memorial State Park and was permanently excluded from all Departmen=
t volunteer programs in a letter dated March 26, 2025.



The period requested is February 1, 2025 to the present.



I request the following records concerning me, held by or sent or received =
by Director Lisa Sumption and Deputy Director J.R. Collier.



1. All communications concerning me sent or received by Director Lisa Sumpt=
ion, in any medium, including email, text message, instant message, and any=
 messaging application, on any device or account used for Department busine=
ss.



2. All communications concerning me sent or received by Deputy Director J.R=
. Collier, on the same terms.



3. All communications between Director Sumption and Deputy Director Collier=
 concerning me.



For the purpose of items 1 through 3, "concerning me" includes any communic=
ation referring to Robert White, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White, Sam =
White, rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>, oprdvolunteerabuse.org, rsw=
fire.com, my date of birth, my volunteer service, my dismissal, my exclusio=
n, my correspondence, my public records requests, the March 24, 2026 law en=
forcement contact at my residence, or the legal fund I have opened.



4. All notes, memoranda, summaries, or other records authored by either ind=
ividual concerning me, including handwritten notes and calendar entries.



5. Any record reflecting a direction or instruction given by either individ=
ual concerning me, including any instruction regarding whether or how staff=
 should respond to my correspondence.



This request does not seek records held by any other Department employee. I=
f a communication responsive to items 1 through 3 was sent to or received f=
rom another employee, it is responsive because Director Sumption or Deputy =
Director Collier is a party to it.





Administration



Fee waiver. I request a waiver under ORS 192.324(5). Disclosure primarily b=
enefits the general public. These records concern how the two highest offic=
ials of a state agency handled a documented complaint of retaliation by the=
ir own staff, and the conduct that followed. I have no commercial purpose. =
All records produced will be published in full, at no charge, at oprdvolunt=
eerabuse.org.



Acknowledgment and timeline. ORS 192.324(2) requires acknowledgment or comp=
letion within five business days, and ORS 192.329(5) requires a reasonable =
estimated completion date where a response cannot be completed within fifte=
en business days. I request both in writing.



Fees. ORS 192.324(4) prohibits a fee exceeding $25 without prior written no=
tice. If a fee is to be charged, I request that notice with an itemized bas=
is before any work is performed, and the opportunity to narrow the request =
rather than have it held pending payment. I have no ability to receive or r=
eturn printed forms; any fee waiver determination should not be conditioned=
 on the return of a printed document.



Format. Electronic delivery by email or secure link, in native format with =
headers, recipients, timestamps, metadata, and attachments preserved and in=
tact.



Preservation. Please treat all records responsive to this request as subjec=
t to litigation hold. I have served a notice of tort claim on the State of =
Oregon under ORS 30.275, and the Department of Administrative Services has =
opened claim P195403.



Disposition. For each numbered item, please state whether responsive record=
s exist, produce them, or cite the specific exemption claimed for each reco=
rd or portion withheld, as ORS 192.329(2) requires. If any responsive recor=
d is withheld, identify it by date, author, recipient, and subject.



Robert Samuel White

oprdvolunteerabuse.org



